{"title":"Lua","slug":"Lua","html":"<div class=\"wk-note wk-style\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Wiki note</span></p>\n<p>This tutorial's tone differs from the rest of the wiki.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Lua is a lightweight scripting language written in ANSI <a data-wiki=\"C\" href=\"#/library/C\">C</a>, designed to be easy to port and embed. Being smaller than <a data-wiki=\"Python\" href=\"#/library/Python\">Python</a>, it is also easier to port.</p>\n<h2 id=\"porting\">Porting</h2>\n<p>Download the source code from here: <a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://www.lua.org/download.html\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.lua.org/download.html</a> Then, modify src/Makefile (not the Makefile at the root).</p>\n<p>Change the variable CC to the target OS <a data-wiki=\"GCC Cross-Compiler\" href=\"#/library/GCC_Cross_Compiler\">cross compiler</a>, e.g.</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode makefile\"><code class=\"sourceCode makefile\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><span class=\"dt\">CC</span> <span class=\"ch\">=</span><span class=\"st\"> x86_64-elf-gcc -std=gnu99</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Depending on the target OS level of POSIX-ness, include and library directories maybe have to be changed.</p>\n<p>Lua depends on the following C standard library functions. Some of them can be just stubs (like the time-related functions).</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb2\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb2-1\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> isalnum<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-2\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> iscntrl<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-3\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> isgraph<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-4\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> islower<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-5\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> isprint<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-6\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> ispunct<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-7\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> isupper<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-8\"><span class=\"dt\">int</span> isxdigit<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">int</span> c<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-9\">__attribute__<span class=\"op\">((</span>noreturn<span class=\"op\">))</span> <span class=\"dt\">void</span> abort<span class=\"op\">();</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-10\"><span class=\"dt\">double</span> acos<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">double</span> x<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-11\"><span class=\"dt\">double</span> asin<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">double</span> x<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-12\"><span class=\"dt\">double</span> atan2<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">double</span> y<span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dt\">double</span> x<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-13\"><span class=\"dt\">double</span> ceil<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">double</span> x<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-14\"><span class=\"dt\">void</span> clearerr<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">FILE</span> <span class=\"op\">*</span>stream<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-15\">clock_t clock<span class=\"op\">();</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-16\"><span class=\"dt\">double</span> cos<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">double</span> x<span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-17\"><span class=\"dt\